{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-stable-atom","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:stable-atom","kind":"definition","title":"Stable atom (Frobenius positivity of the normal form)","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-atom-knot"],"tags":["stability","ilp","lp-dual","atom","frobenius-positivity"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.BraidKnot.StableAtom","text":"stable-atom.md","leanSource":"stable-atom.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:stable-atom\"></a><p><em>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">K</code> be an atom-knot (<a href=\"#def:atom-knot\" data-at=\"knots-particles-confinement/atom-isotope-knots\">atom</a>) with normal form <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T_w \\in H_{n(K)}(q)</code>. Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{G}(q)</code> be the Frobenius Gram matrix of the primitive Wedderburn-block operators <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\{e_\\lambda\\}_{\\lambda \\vdash k,\\;k \\leq k_{\\max}}</code>. Decompose the normal form in the primitive basis:</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  T_w\n  \\;=\\;\n  \\sum_\\lambda x_\\lambda \\cdot e_\\lambda,\n  \\qquad\n  x_\\lambda \\in \\mathbb{Z}_{\\geq 0}.</code></pre>\n<p><em>The coefficient vector <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">x(K, q) := (x_\\lambda)_\\lambda</code> is determined by <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T_w</code>. The atom <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">K</code> is <strong>stable at <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code></strong> if and only if this vector is an integer point of the positivity cone:</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  x(K, q) \\in \\mathbb{Z}_{\\geq 0}^N\n  \\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n  \\mathrm{G}(q) \\, x(K, q) \\;\\geq\\; 0\n  \\;\\text{coordinatewise.}</code></pre>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/stable-atom.md","heading":"Definition","number":"9.10.9","page":"b/def-stable-atom","qa":{"counts":{"pass":79,"fail":1,"warn":0,"na":11,"unknown":0,"stale":65},"milnor":{"total":2,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BraidKnot.StableAtom","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/stable-atom.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
